### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

core

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description

We we use a directive in `hostDirectives` and on host element, two instances are created:

```ts
@Directive({
	selector: '[appTest]',
	standalone: true,
})
class TestDirective {
	constructor() {
		console.log('TestDirective'); // logs two times
	}
}

@Component({
	selector: 'app-test',
	template: 'test',
	standalone: true,
	hostDirectives: [TestDirective], // <-- here
})
class TestComponent {}

@Component({
	selector: 'app-host',
	template: '<app-test appTest></app-test>',
        //                   ^^^^^^^ and here
	standalone: true,
	imports: [TestComponent, TestDirective],
})
class HostComponent {}
```

But if I add an input to the previous directive, I can no longer use it in `HostElement`. Event if `TestComponent` does not expose `TestDirective`'s inputs:

```ts
@Directive({
	selector: '[appTest]',
	standalone: true,
})
class TestDirective implements OnInit {
	@Input() appTest: string;

	ngOnInit() {
		console.log('TestDirective', this.appTest); // logs two times, once with 321 and once with undefined
	}
}

@Component({
	selector: 'app-test',
	template: 'test',
	standalone: true,
	hostDirectives: [TestDirective],
})
class TestComponent {
	constructor() {
		inject(TestDirective).appTest = 321;
	}
}

@Component({
	selector: 'app-host',
	template: '<app-test [appTest]="123"></app-test>',
       //                    ^^^^^^^^^ NG0303: Can't bind to 'appTest' since it isn't a known property of 'app-test'
	standalone: true,
	imports: [TestComponent, TestDirective],
})
class HostComponent {}
```

A more realistic example is with `NgClass`. When you have many classes with dynamic names, it is easier to use a `NgClass` hostDirective than to use a `HostBinding('class')`. But doing so prevent the consumer of the component to use `ngClass` on it.

### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug

https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-sezuuc?file=src%2Fmain.ts,src%2Fwith-input.ts,src%2Fwithout-input.ts

### Please provide the exception or error you saw

```true
core.mjs:6203 NG0303: Can't bind to 'appTest' since it isn't a known property of 'app-test' (used in the 'HostComponent' component template).
1. If 'app-test' is an Angular component and it has the 'appTest' input, then verify that it is included in the '@Component.imports' of this component.
2. If 'app-test' is a Web Component then add 'CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA' to the '@Component.schemas' of this component to suppress this message.
3. To allow any property add 'NO_ERRORS_SCHEMA' to the '@Component.schemas' of this component.
```
